The quoted CI half-width is 0.3365 pp, implying an effective n ~ 72,000; the own CI half-width at n = 194 is 7.22 pp (normal approximation 6.48 pp). No row-level bootstrap over <= 276 rows can yield a +/-0.34 pp interval, and 69.399% is not an attainable integer fraction (97/0.69399 = 139.77; no k/n with n <= 300 equals it). The quoted level therefore belongs to the reference implementation's own cleaned/weighted dataset; this file reproduces its RANKING, not its absolute value.

## 5. Verdict
**Interviews** is the most commonly used elicitation technique: 50.000% (97/194, 95% CI [42.78, 57.22]), ahead of Scenarios and Prototyping (38.660% each), Workshops/Meetings (38.144%) and Observation (32.990%). Interviews is the top-ranked named technique under all 10 sensitivity specs; the paired bootstrap gap to the runners-up is 11.34 pp (one-sided p-hat ~ 0.011-0.014; McNemar exact p ~ 0.014-0.017), i.e. significant at the 5% level but with limited margin (the paired 95% CI lower bound is only ~1.0-2.1 pp).

## 6. Variables and the relation relied upon
Columns: Q9_ML_Elicitation_Interviews, _Scenarios, _Prototyping, _Workshops_Meetings, _Observation, _Others, _Others_Free, plus Status (quality audit).
Relation: negative codes -> structural missingness -> valid denominator (276 -> 194) -> absolute percentages of all techniques change -> ordering between techniques is unchanged.
